  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_JVM_MODES='full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_JVM_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1444-nominal-jvm-installed-ordinary-full-r1-output' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_JVM_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_JVM_TEST='1' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' '/usr/bin/node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' 'tests/helpers/nominal-subtype-jvm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce the complete Maven JAR and POM. Author sources are removed before offline installation. Unchanged Java and Kotlin callers replay after moving the installed consumer tree and again after deleting all consumer sources, for six executions per selection. The full fixture checks per-use constructor selection and normalization, repeated record fields, active variant branches, aliases, mixed Fin guards, exact rejection paths, caller-input preservation and recovery. Kotlin nullability and compiled invalid-caller probes have separate retained checks. Nominal acceptance covers the tested Nat Subtype records, variants, aliases and copied constructor-free results with JDK 22.0.2 and Kotlin 2.2.0 through offline Maven-package installation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. Java and Kotlin consumers run after relocation and again after removal of all consumer sources. Other primitive-base nominal fixtures and other hosts need separate acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain pending. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured; these local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance. The repository archive retains non-native JAR members, compiled validation probes, receipts and source snapshots, but not the native library, complete JARs or consumer bytecode. The complete JDK and Kotlin distributions remain trusted tools.",
